# Cloudflare Static Assets redirects. Copied verbatim into dist/ at build time,
# exactly like public/_headers.
#
# Only conventional-path aliases belong here. Trailing-slash normalisation is
# NOT in this file: Cloudflare's own html_handling performs it, as a 307 whose
# status code is not configurable. DO NOT try to turn it into a 301 via this
# file — attempted 2026-09-21 with one exact `/x  /x/  301` rule per built
# directory (536 rules, no wildcards): the deploy was rejected at version
# creation with "Maximum number of dynamic _redirects rules limit of 100
# exceeded [code: 100324]". Why a wildcard-free rule counted as dynamic: per
# wrangler's own parser (canCreateStaticRule in parseRedirects, and again when
# it builds the manifest — node_modules/wrangler/wrangler-dist/cli.js), a rule
# is static ONLY while no splat or placeholder rule appears above it; once the
# first dynamic rule is seen, every rule after it is dynamic too. Those 536
# were appended below the splats, so all of them hit the 100-rule dynamic cap.
# Here only /sitemap.xml is static; everything else is dynamic, so treat the
# file as a budget of 100 rules in total and never automate additions to it
# (src/lib/redirects.test.ts caps it at 60). Google follows 307s and
# consolidates signals across them; the 301 was never worth that budget.

# robots.txt advertises /sitemap-index.xml, but /sitemap.xml is the path humans
# and third-party tools guess first, and it returned a 404.
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap-index.xml  301

# Cloudflare Static Assets are case-sensitive, so the natural BCP-47 spelling of
# the Brazilian Portuguese tree (/pt-BR/) 404s while the built path is /pt-br/.
# Nothing on the site links it, but hreflang codes and hand-typed URLs use it.
/pt-BR/*  /pt-br/:splat  301

# /learn, /mission-90, /tests and /changelog are English-only by design
# (ENGLISH_ONLY_SECTIONS in src/i18n/paths.ts), so localizeNavHref links them
# unprefixed from every locale and no /de/learn/ page is ever built. A visitor
# who hand-prefixes one — or an external link that does — hit a 404; send them
# to the English original instead.
/de/learn/*         /learn/:splat         301
/de/mission-90/*    /mission-90/:splat    301
/de/tests/*         /tests/:splat         301
/de/changelog/*     /changelog/:splat     301
/es/learn/*         /learn/:splat         301
/es/mission-90/*    /mission-90/:splat    301
/es/tests/*         /tests/:splat         301
/es/changelog/*     /changelog/:splat     301
/fr/learn/*         /learn/:splat         301
/fr/mission-90/*    /mission-90/:splat    301
/fr/tests/*         /tests/:splat         301
/fr/changelog/*     /changelog/:splat     301
/pt-br/learn/*      /learn/:splat         301
/pt-br/mission-90/* /mission-90/:splat    301
/pt-br/tests/*      /tests/:splat         301
/pt-br/changelog/*  /changelog/:splat     301

# Google Search Console's 404 export of 2026-09-26 (105 URLs, kept as
# src/lib/fixtures/gsc-404-2026-09.txt) is almost entirely localized category
# and tag pages that were once built and are not any more: localized
# /tools/<category>/ and /blog/tag/<tag>/ copies were evaluated and rejected as
# thin near-duplicates, and the English equivalents exist. These use a ':x'
# placeholder, NOT a splat: '/de/tools/*' would also match the live /de/tools/
# hub, because a splat may be empty while ':x' is [^/]+. Redirects run before
# the asset lookup, so a rule that matches a live page replaces it.
# src/lib/redirects.test.ts proves no rule here matches a live localized route.
/de/tools/:cat/         /tools/:cat/          301
/de/tools/:cat          /tools/:cat/          301
/de/blog/tag/:tag/      /blog/tag/:tag/       301
/de/blog/tag/:tag       /blog/tag/:tag/       301
/es/tools/:cat/         /tools/:cat/          301
/es/tools/:cat          /tools/:cat/          301
/es/blog/tag/:tag/      /blog/tag/:tag/       301
/es/blog/tag/:tag       /blog/tag/:tag/       301
/fr/tools/:cat/         /tools/:cat/          301
/fr/tools/:cat          /tools/:cat/          301
/fr/blog/tag/:tag/      /blog/tag/:tag/       301
/fr/blog/tag/:tag       /blog/tag/:tag/       301
/pt-br/tools/:cat/      /tools/:cat/          301
/pt-br/tools/:cat       /tools/:cat/          301
/pt-br/blog/tag/:tag/   /blog/tag/:tag/       301
/pt-br/blog/tag/:tag    /blog/tag/:tag/       301
